# What belongs in evidence/ and what does not.
#
# docs/methodology/experiments.md: an experiment "does not clean up its own
# output ... the evidence is the point". The evidence that is KEPT is the
# script plus the RESULT it printed, both tracked. What is ignored is the
# regenerable intermediate: object files, unpacked sources, synthetic root
# filesystems, raw straces, and the BUILT ARTEFACTS themselves.
#
# ⛔ A BUILT BINARY IS NOT EVIDENCE, IT IS OUTPUT. Committing them put 161 MiB
# into this repository -- a 46 MiB static CPython and its 98 MiB standard
# library among them -- for artefacts that `sh poc/<name>/run.sh` recreates
# byte for byte from a sha256-pinned tarball. The RESULT.txt beside them
# records what they did, which is the part a later session cannot regenerate.

evidence/*/build/
evidence/*/*.trace
evidence/poc/*/build/

# POC build artefacts: the binaries, their staged data trees, and build logs.
evidence/poc/*/pystdlib/
evidence/poc/*/ext/
evidence/poc/*/gawk
evidence/poc/*/nano
evidence/poc/*/curl
evidence/poc/*/jq
evidence/poc/*/python3
evidence/poc/*/terminfo-probe
evidence/poc/*/*-make.log
evidence/poc/*/*-configure.log
evidence/poc/*/*-install.log
evidence/poc/*/make.log
evidence/poc/*/configure.log
evidence/poc/*/install.log
evidence/poc/*/probe-build.log

# Root filesystems live outside the tree by default ($PGB_ROOTFS_DIR).
/rootfs/

/tool/target/
*.o
*.so.tmp

# 62-'s staged upstream artefacts: sharun, appimagetool, uruntime, mkdwarfs and
# the AppImages built from them. All are re-fetched by digest and rebuilt by
# the experiment; ⛔ A BUILT BINARY IS NOT EVIDENCE, IT IS OUTPUT.
evidence/*/*.AppImage
evidence/*/AppDir*/
